{
  "dom_id": "step-q342834",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "$$\n\nCalculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}  $-\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{x{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}$",
  "worked_solution": "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAnd the quotient rule is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}(\\frac{u}{v})}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule, chain rule, and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2})}^{′}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{({x}^{2})}^{2}}\\cdot {({x}^{2})}^{′}-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{4}}\\cdot 2x-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{x{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{(1-{x}^{4})\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{x{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
